<title>EGYPT: Misr Hotels 95/96 net profit up 39 pct.</title>
<headline>Misr Hotels 95/96 net profit up 39 pct.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-10-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Misr Hotels net profit rose 39 percent in the 1995/96 financial year to 29 million pounds ($8.5 million) from 20.8 million pounds in the previous year, according to unaudited figures made available on Saturday.</p>
<p>The financial year ends on June 30.</p>
<p>Misr Hotels, in which the state holds a majority stake, owns the Hilton and other hotels in Egypt.</p>
<p>($1 = 3.40 pounds)</p>
<p>Cairo newsroom + 20 2 578-3290/1.</p>
</text>
